  "notes": [
    "The source reports transcription errors at 5C, 6C, 5H (labeling, corrected here) and 2G; there, sRGB 58/88/159 was used instead of 99/86/156 according to a reader's note, which fits Lab better.",
    "User's model: SCK300 (according to retailer pages identical to the SCK310 with a different case; 4 cards, 62 color targets in total). That the 48 color fields are identical to the SpyderCheckr 48 is likely but not proven.",
    "Layout (visually confirmed on a photo of an SCK300): two color cards in portrait orientation, 4 columns x 6 rows each. Card 1 = columns A-D, card 2 = columns E-H; the letter of the ID is the column, the digit the row (from the top, 1-6). column and row count from 0 from the left and top respectively. The color values themselves remain unconfirmed.",
    "\"check\" is dE76 between the given Lab and the Lab computed from sRGB (D65->D50), only as a plausibility test."
  ],
